  have comments from the director of the  final season as well as the voice actor  for erin and so looking at the  director's statement first he says thank  you for waiting the final season part  two will start in january next year from  the large-scale battle in shiganshina to  the origin story of the titans we are  finally approaching the climax we are  also taking on many new challenges in  terms of images and how that scene will  be visualized please look forward to it  so that comment there about the uh the  challenges of the new images if you're a  mangrove you know this but the attacker  type of manga in terms of art it gets  very complex towards the end there are  certain things that will be very  difficult to animate and i think that's  what the director is referring to  because uh yeah things will get way more  difficult to animate than they did in  the first half of the season so this is  just me speculating but i imagine the  second part will be quite cgi heavy  because if we look back in the first  half there was a decent amount of cgi  even though um it wasn't nearly as  complex as what they need to animate for  the second half so again there's gonna  be a lot of cgi but i think it's  practical i definitely prefer it when  the titans are in 2d but i also  understand why sometimes it needs to be  3d and all that because yeah this stuff  is just it's not easy it's not easy at  all so uh i don't envy the people that  do have to animate this but i'm sure  when it comes out next year it would be  great  for the voice actor for aaron he only  made one statement and that was if you  don't fight you can't win and yeah that  was it short and sweet nice and simple  and uh yeah yeah so looking forward to  it january 2022 is when the uh the  second half of the season resumes and if  you haven't seen already then do be sure  to check out my reviews for the first  half of the season for pretty much every  episode except the very first one i  broke it down you know r